#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available file formats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "&parley; can read and write the following file formats:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"its native xml-style document type with the extension <literal role="
"\"extension\">.kvtml</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to share documents with others, use this format as it is the "
"only file format that is capable of storing <emphasis>all</emphasis> "
"properties in &parley;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"simple text files with special delimiters between the entries which are also "
"used by simple database programs. The extension is <literal role=\"extension"
"\">.csv</literal> in this case."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a lot of files on the Internet which use the tab stops or one or "
"two colons to separate the languages. To select this separator use the tab "
"for setting the <link linkend=\"general-settings\"><guilabel>Open/Save</"
"guilabel> options</link> in the <guilabel>General</guilabel> page of the "
"<guilabel>Configure - &parley;</guilabel> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; reads the first few bytes of a file and guesses its file format. If "
"none of the special types like <literal role=\"extension\">.kvtml</literal> "
"or <literal role=\"extension\">.lex</literal> are recognized, it will try "
"the <literal role=\"extension\">.csv</literal> format."
msgstr ""

